The following skills are forks of Superpowers skills, rewritten around a tuckit
board: what upstream writes into markdown files lands on a slice instead, and
the forks that produce no artifact of their own govern what the others may
claim.

  shared/skills/designing-a-slice/      <- skills/brainstorming
  shared/skills/executing-a-slice/      <- skills/executing-plans
  shared/skills/shipping-a-slice/       <- skills/finishing-a-development-branch
  shared/skills/requesting-a-review/    <- skills/requesting-code-review
  shared/skills/receiving-a-review/     <- skills/receiving-code-review
  shared/skills/verifying-before-claiming/  <- skills/verification-before-completion

requesting-a-review carries two review prompts forked from Superpowers'
skills/subagent-driven-development (task-reviewer-prompt.md ->
reviewer-prompt.md, and re-review-prompt.md).

Superpowers' four remaining skills are not forked here: using-git-worktrees and
dispatching-parallel-agents, which are being forked next, and using-superpowers
and writing-skills, which are Superpowers' own meta-tooling for finding and
authoring skills and have no counterpart here. This plugin is meant to replace
Superpowers rather than run alongside it, so it does not defer to them by name;
until the first two are forked, the layers they cover are simply absent.
